course: dictionary
lesson: 6186
title: Long words for stealing money
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: Some long words sound important but hide a simple idea. Misappropriation is one of them. It means taking money or property that someone trusted you to look after, and using it wrongly for yourself. «"Misappropriation of funds" means stealing money that one was trusted to look after, such as a club's treasurer taking it.»
explain: Look at the clues. Trusted and look after tell you the money was never really yours to keep. A treasurer is the person who looks after a club's money, so a treasurer who spends it on themselves is committing misappropriation. Try the swap test: put "stealing money someone trusted you with" into the sentence, and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Be careful, because formal writers sometimes use long words to make bad news sound smaller. Officials may write «misappropriation of funds» where you would simply say stealing money. The long phrase describes the same wrong thing, just in stiff, formal clothes. Plain words often tell the truth more clearly.
fact: Misappropriation is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say "some misappropriation", not "a misappropriation".
fact: The verb is misappropriate: to misappropriate money means to use it wrongly for yourself.
fact: «Misappropriation of funds» is a common phrase in news reports and law.
fact: A treasurer is the person who looks after a club's or group's money.
fact: Officials sometimes use long words such as "irregularities" for fraud, so read formal language carefully.
exercise: «The club treasurer spent the club's money on a new car for herself.» What is this an example of? | A kind donation | *Misappropriation of funds | A club dinner | A fair prize
exercise: Officials write «misappropriation of funds» in a report. What does the phrase mean in plain English? | *Stealing money someone trusted you to look after | Lending money to a friend | Counting money carefully | Spending money at a party
exercise: What does a treasurer do? | Writes the club's songs | Cooks lunch for the club | Coaches the team | *Looks after the club's money
test: The verb misappropriate means which of these? | To count money twice | To give money to charity | To hide money in a box | *To use money wrongly for yourself
test: Which sentence uses misappropriation correctly? | *The inquiry found misappropriation of the charity's funds. | The misappropriation was a bright red bicycle. | Misappropriation is a sunny day. | She misappropriation the cake at lunch.
exam: Officials write "irregularities" and "misappropriation of funds" instead of plain words. What is the best reason to read such phrases carefully? | *They can hide a simple wrong, like stealing | They are the names of colours | They always mean something good | They are only used in poems
